# No catch-all rewrite to /index.html.
#
# This used to be: /*  /index.html  200
#
# That rule made Cloudflare serve the homepage shell for EVERY url, which both
# hid the prerendered pages and told Google that every address was really the
# homepage. With the SPA now prerendered, real files exist for every route, so
# the rewrite is removed and each URL serves its own document. Unknown URLs now
# return a genuine 404 instead of a 200 serving the homepage (a soft 404).
